1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:15,996
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is May twenty-sixth. Today's story: the man who created Japan's convenience store culture has passed away at ninety-three. Let's listen.

2
00:00:16,596 --> 00:00:32,723
[News] セブンアンドアイホールディングスの名誉顧問、鈴木敏文さんが、五月十八日に亡くなりました。九十三歳でした。死因は心不全です。

3
00:00:33,423 --> 00:00:47,847
[News] 鈴木さんは、千九百七十四年に、東京の豊洲に、コンビニエンスストアの日本第一号店を出しました。セブンイレブンです。

4
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:59,948
[News] それまで、日本にコンビニはありませんでした。鈴木さんがアメリカのセブンイレブンを日本に持ってきたのです。

5
00:01:00,648 --> 00:01:16,343
[News] 今、日本にはコンビニが約五万六千店あります。セブンイレブン、ローソン、ファミリーマート。日本の生活に欠かせないものになりました。

6
00:01:17,043 --> 00:01:37,587
[News] 鈴木さんは「お客様の立場で考えなさい」といつも言っていました。おにぎり、お弁当、ATM、宅配便の受け取り。コンビニのサービスは、鈴木さんのこの考え方から生まれました。

7
00:01:38,287 --> 00:01:50,144
[News] 二千十六年に会長を退任し、名誉顧問になりました。日本のコンビニ産業の父と呼ばれています。

8
00:01:50,843 --> 00:01:52,475
[Host] Let's break it down.

9
00:01:53,075 --> 00:01:54,852
[Host] The first sentence.

10
00:01:55,451 --> 00:02:06,924
[Slow] セブンアンドアイホールディングスの名誉顧問、鈴木敏文さんが、五月十八日に亡くなりました。

11
00:02:07,724 --> 00:02:16,340
[Host] Suzuki Toshifumi, honorary advisor of Seven and I Holdings, passed away on May eighteenth. Let's look at the key words.

12
00:02:16,939 --> 00:02:19,747
[Vocab] 亡くなりました

13
00:02:20,147 --> 00:02:26,963
[Host] Passed away. This is the polite way to say someone passed away. You'll hear this in news all the time.

14
00:02:27,563 --> 00:02:30,228
[Vocab] 名誉顧問

15
00:02:30,627 --> 00:02:39,243
[Host] Honorary advisor. A title given to retired executives. They no longer run the company, but they keep an advisory role.

16
00:02:39,843 --> 00:02:41,427
[Host] Next sentence.

17
00:02:42,027 --> 00:02:53,644
[Slow] 千九百七十四年に、東京の豊洲に、コンビニエンスストアの日本第一号店を出しました。

18
00:02:54,443 --> 00:03:01,500
[Host] In nineteen seventy-four, he opened the first convenience store in Japan, in Toyosu, Tokyo.

19
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:05,099
[Vocab] 第一号店

20
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:11,451
[Host] Store number one. The very first store. You'll see this pattern for other firsts too.

21
00:03:12,051 --> 00:03:14,139
[Vocab] 出す

22
00:03:14,539 --> 00:03:21,500
[Host] It literally means to put out. But here it means to open a store. The meaning shifts depending on context.

23
00:03:22,099 --> 00:03:24,139
[Host] Why was this such a big deal?

24
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:30,548
[Slow] それまで、日本にコンビニはありませんでした。

25
00:03:31,348 --> 00:03:37,828
[Host] Until then, there were no convenience stores in Japan. He brought the whole concept from America.

26
00:03:38,427 --> 00:03:40,780
[Vocab] それまで

27
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:47,731
[Host] Until then. A very useful time expression. It points back to a time you already mentioned.

28
00:03:48,331 --> 00:03:50,756
[Host] How big are convenience stores today?

29
00:03:51,355 --> 00:03:58,292
[Slow] 今、日本にはコンビニが約五万六千店あります。

30
00:03:59,092 --> 00:04:04,036
[Host] Today, there are approximately fifty-six thousand convenience stores in Japan.

31
00:04:04,635 --> 00:04:06,675
[Vocab] 約

32
00:04:07,075 --> 00:04:14,780
[Host] Approximately. Short, common, and very useful. You'll hear it constantly in news whenever numbers come up.

33
00:04:15,379 --> 00:04:17,396
[Host] And what they mean to Japan.

34
00:04:17,995 --> 00:04:23,660
[Slow] 日本の生活に欠かせないものになりました。

35
00:04:24,459 --> 00:04:27,819
[Host] They became something indispensable to life in Japan.

36
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:30,939
[Vocab] 欠かせない

37
00:04:31,339 --> 00:04:37,339
[Host] Indispensable, can't do without. A strong word. Very common in news.

38
00:04:37,939 --> 00:04:40,100
[Host] His famous philosophy.

39
00:04:40,699 --> 00:04:45,283
[Slow] お客様の立場で考えなさい。

40
00:04:46,084 --> 00:04:53,067
[Host] Think from the customer's perspective. This one sentence explains why Japanese convenience stores are so good.

41
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:55,875
[Vocab] 立場

42
00:04:56,276 --> 00:05:02,228
[Host] Standpoint, perspective. A very common word. You can use it for anything.

43
00:05:02,827 --> 00:05:04,483
[Host] And the final line.

44
00:05:05,084 --> 00:05:10,867
[Slow] 日本のコンビニ産業の父と呼ばれています。

45
00:05:11,668 --> 00:05:15,435
[Host] He is called the father of Japan's convenience store industry.

46
00:05:16,036 --> 00:05:18,411
[Vocab] 産業

47
00:05:18,812 --> 00:05:24,740
[Host] Industry. A formal word, mostly used in news and business contexts.

48
00:05:25,339 --> 00:05:28,196
[Vocab] 呼ばれています

49
00:05:28,596 --> 00:05:35,675
[Host] Is being called. This is the passive form plus the ongoing state. A natural way to say is known as.

50
00:05:36,276 --> 00:05:39,276
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

51
00:05:39,875 --> 00:05:56,004
[News] セブンアンドアイホールディングスの名誉顧問、鈴木敏文さんが、五月十八日に亡くなりました。九十三歳でした。死因は心不全です。

52
00:05:56,704 --> 00:06:11,127
[News] 鈴木さんは、千九百七十四年に、東京の豊洲に、コンビニエンスストアの日本第一号店を出しました。セブンイレブンです。

53
00:06:11,827 --> 00:06:23,228
[News] それまで、日本にコンビニはありませんでした。鈴木さんがアメリカのセブンイレブンを日本に持ってきたのです。

54
00:06:23,927 --> 00:06:39,624
[News] 今、日本にはコンビニが約五万六千店あります。セブンイレブン、ローソン、ファミリーマート。日本の生活に欠かせないものになりました。

55
00:06:40,324 --> 00:07:00,867
[News] 鈴木さんは「お客様の立場で考えなさい」といつも言っていました。おにぎり、お弁当、ATM、宅配便の受け取り。コンビニのサービスは、鈴木さんのこの考え方から生まれました。

56
00:07:01,567 --> 00:07:13,423
[News] 二千十六年に会長を退任し、名誉顧問になりました。日本のコンビニ産業の父と呼ばれています。

57
00:07:14,124 --> 00:07:16,860
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

58
00:07:17,459 --> 00:07:24,444
[Slow] 鈴木さんは何年にコンビニの第一号店を出しましたか？

59
00:07:25,244 --> 00:07:29,995
[Host] What year did he open the first convenience store? Nineteen seventy-four.

60
00:07:30,596 --> 00:07:36,235
[Slow] 今、日本にコンビニは何店ありますか？

61
00:07:37,036 --> 00:07:42,795
[Host] How many convenience stores are there in Japan today? Approximately fifty-six thousand.

62
00:07:43,396 --> 00:07:48,507
[Slow] 鈴木さんはいつも何と言っていましたか？

63
00:07:49,307 --> 00:07:53,339
[Host] What did he always say? Think from the customer's perspective.

64
00:07:53,939 --> 00:07:55,860
[Host] Vocabulary recap.

65
00:07:56,459 --> 00:07:59,267
[Vocab] 亡くなりました

66
00:07:59,668 --> 00:08:01,036
[Host] Passed away.

67
00:08:01,636 --> 00:08:04,300
[Vocab] 名誉顧問

68
